 gto.com/events/2026/06/06/original_image5c8a5e4b-715b-4e43-8d38-5c57e29202
 43.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Whether it’s improv or scripted sketch comedy\, putting your
  scenes in the right order can make or break a show - the difference betwe
 en a show that builds from laugh to laugh and continually surprises and de
 lights the audience\, or one that loses momentum and limps to the finish l
 ine. In this one-of-a-kind workshop\, Veteran Second City director\, write
 r-performer\, and teacher Chris Earle shares his 3 decades of experience a
 nd insights into the art and science of building a great Running Order\, i
 nviting participants to solve the puzzle of building their own RO’s with
  a series of fun and challenging hands-on exercises.\nCOST: $100 + Tax
LOCATION:Comedy Bar East
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/all-killer-no-filler-the-art-of-the-runn
 ing-order-with-chris-earle-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:An ICU Open Mic
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260614T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260614T210000
UID:blogto-235943@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/02/original_image0d56cb5e-e138-4051-8638-eee81c996b
 3b.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Pay-what-you-want open mic featuring 4-minute sets\, surprise 
 pro comic drop-ins\, and a paid spot for the night’s best performer.\n
 🎤 ICU OPEN MIC – PAY WHAT YOU WANT 🎤\nLooking for an open mic in T
 oronto where everyone is welcome?\nJoin us for ICU Open Mic\, an inclusive
 \, accessible\, pay-what-you-want showcase featuring comedians\, musicians
 \, poets\, storytellers\, first-time performers\, and surprise professiona
 l comic drop-ins.\nWhether you’re stepping on stage for the very first t
 ime or you’re a seasoned performer working on new material\, ICU Open Mi
 c provides a supportive environment where all talent is welcome.\n🎭 Fou
 r-Minute Sets\n🪣 Bucket Show Format\n🌟 Surprise Pro Comic Drop-Ins\n
 🏆 Best Set of the Night Wins a Paid Spot on Laughs Without Limits\n💰
  Pay What You Want Admission\n♿ Fully Accessible Venue\nNo cliques. No g
 atekeepers. No endless waiting. Just a room full of performers\, creators\
 , comedy fans\, and people who love live entertainment.\nEVENT DETAILS\n
 📅 Sunday\, June 14\n📍 Sweet Action Theatre180 Shaw Street\, Toronto\
 n📝 Sign-Up: 7:00 PM – 7:30 PM\n🎤 Showtime: 7:30 PM – 9:00 PM\nAB
 OUT ICU OPEN MIC\nPresented by Disability Privilege\, ICU Open Mic was cre
 ated to provide an inclusive performance space where artists of all backgr
 ounds\, abilities\, and experience levels can share their talents.\nOur go
 al is simple: create a welcoming room where people feel comfortable taking
  creative risks\, building confidence\, connecting with audiences\, and ha
 ving fun.\nAudience members are welcome too. Come discover new talent\, su
 pport local performers\, and enjoy an unpredictable night of live entertai
 nment.\nShow up. Go up.\nWe can’t wait to see you there.
LOCATION:Sweet Action Theatre
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/an-icu-open-mic-toronto-3/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
