BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Collective Soundmapping - Guardian & Youth Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260614T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260614T154500
UID:blogto-235575@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/26/original_image8382ca8a-d47a-4a0e-b6b4-226ca3eacc
 26.jpg
DESCRIPTION:This workshop\, focusing on youth and accompanying guardians\,
  aims to listen and collaboratively reflect on land and urban soundscapes 
 through the creative practice of soundmapping.\nThe workshop will begin at
  St. Matthew’s Clubhouse and includes guided exercises through Riverdale
  Park East. Participants will be led through a variety of creative activit
 ies in which they will be asked to listen\, write\, and draw the sounds th
 at we encounter. This workshop will involve soundwalking through the park\
 , with moments to rest\, draw\, and share reflections with each other.\nPa
 rticipants are encouraged to dress comfortably. We will be sitting in the 
 grass at various points\; participants may choose to bring a small mat or 
 blanket to carry with them for sitting.\nIdeally there will be one guardia
 n to each youth participant\, though guardians can register additional you
 ths.\nPWYCA $10 to $20 for accompanying adult guardians & all youths (unde
 r 16) are free. Adults should have a paid ticket for themselves and a free
  ticket for each youth they are accompanying.
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/collective-soundmapping-guardian-youth-w
 orkshop-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
