BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jennifer Bettencourt: Fado Distilled
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260614T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260614T190000
UID:blogto-235914@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/02/original_imagee975f4f8-8eaa-4105-a7bb-8af7c3e871
 22.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Sunday\, June 14 at Reid's Distillery\, Luso-Canadian fadista 
 Jennifer Bettencourt aims to transport you to Lisbon with the evocative bl
 ues of Portugal--fado. Born in the heart of Lisbon's historic neighbourhoo
 ds and lovingly brought to Toronto for all audiences to enjoy\, experience
  Portuguese folk music rich with history and timeless emotions. Accompanie
 d by skilled guitarists Hernani Raposo and Valdemar Mejdoubi\, plus a spec
 ial surprise guest\, Jennifer expertly blends the traditional bittersweet 
 essence of "saudade" with the modernity of an artist fervently keeping the
  flame of fado burning. Spend your Sunday on a passionate Iberian journey 
 in a Canadian "tasca"\, regardless of whether or not you understand Portug
 uese\, and let the universal language of song wash you away into a sea of 
 emotions. Tickets are $15 (+tax and fees) in advance and $20 (+tax and fee
 s) at the door.
LOCATION:Reid's Distillery
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/jennifer-bettencourt-fado-distilled-toro
 nto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:John Lilly and the Earth Coincidence Control Office
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260614T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260614T143700
UID:blogto-235041@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/14/original_image742a96c3-d467-4fbe-88a6-05632cd846
 62.jpg
DESCRIPTION:“One of the most consistently inventive\, impossible-to-cate
 gorize directors of our time\, Almereyda has shown a fascination with visi
 onary characters across both his narrative and documentary films” – Th
 e Criterion Channel\nThe daring experimenter Dr. John C. Lilly dedicated h
 is life to radical self-investigation and unlocking the mysteries of consc
 iousness and communication. “My body is my laboratory” was the motto\,
  and his research on the language of dolphins and whales—as well as psyc
 hedelics and sensory deprivation—assured his own cult status in 20th-cen
 tury pop culture as the basis for Ken Russell’s Altered States and Mike 
 Nichols’s The Day of the Dolphin.\nDirectors Michael Almareyda and Court
 ney Stephens\, along with narrator Chloë Sevigny\, explore the life of a 
 determined scientist and his experiments into the psychonautical unknown.
LOCATION:Hot Docs Cinema
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/john-lilly-and-the-earth-coincidence-con
 trol-office-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
