BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:QHC Kiki in the Park: Trans\, NB\, 2Sprit Sharing Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260614T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260614T180000
UID:blogto-236012@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/03/original_imagef90365f8-b1ee-4b16-bbd3-209898e821
 00.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Join our very first peer support drop-in catered for the trans
 \, nb and two-spirt folks\, with gently moderated conversation while we re
 lax at the park. Every conversation is invitational\, no pressure to answe
 r or share if you’d prefer to just be.\nThe conversation will be moderat
 ed by our partner Caelus Dewi (he/they)\, a gay trans man peer supporter. 
 Be cozy and bring some blankets\, snacks\, and journal!\n📅 Date & Time:
  Thurs June 18\, 6:30-8pm\n📍Location: Brickford Park (local cafe if rai
 n or heat warning)\n🎟 Tickets: Free\, donation suggested $5\nWhat to br
 ing?Attendees are invited to bring water\, a cushion\, picnic blanket or f
 oldable chair if needed! Feel free to bring some snacks to share around to
 o!\nCommunity Partner:\nCaelus Dewi (he/they) is a gay trans man peer supp
 orter with experience providing 1 on 1 online and anonymous peer support w
 ith LGBT Youthline\, and group peer support for trans and queer students a
 t Humber College. Outside of queer and trans peer support work\, Caelus wo
 rks in wellness spaces in Toronto and believes in healing via community.\n
 “I firmly believe each of us have the capacity to make our own decisions
  in our lives. This is why my approach focuses on building confidence in d
 ecision making through peer support and active listening.”
LOCATION:Bickford Park
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/qhc-kiki-in-the-park-trans-nb-2sprit-sha
 ring-circle-toronto/
