BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Master the Art of Calm within the ChAoS
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260616T191500
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260616T204500
UID:blogto-236441@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/11/original_imagedc81d0d8-b14d-4830-86c4-82fbccfd59
 cb.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Try Practical Stoic Philosophy - Cultivate Strength\, Serenity
  and Service!\nWe live in a time of great opportunity - but also constant 
 noise and distraction.\nThere is more access than ever before to knowledge
 \, connection\, and possibilities for growth. Yet many of us feel pulled i
 n too many directions: endless notifications\, constant novelty\, superfic
 ial trends and pressure to keep up. Attention is scattered. Depth is easil
 y lost.\nLife also brings unexpected inner struggles\, relationship challe
 nges\, and moments that ask more of us than we feel ready to give. Beyond 
 our personal lives\, we also witness a world shaped by uncertainty\, rapid
  change\, violence\, anxiety\, and division.\nHow can we remain steady\, j
 oyful\, and purposeful in the middle of it all?\nMaster the Art of Calm Wi
 thin the Chaos is a practical and inspiring workshop to help us discover h
 ow ancient Stoic philosophy can help us live our modern life with greater 
 clarity\, joy\, resilience and purpose.\nAt its heart\, Stoicism is not ab
 out becoming cold or detached. It is a spiritual philosophy of discovering
  the laws of life and living in harmony with them. It invites us to cultiv
 ate character\, become calm within\, and act with wisdom so we can all ser
 ve the common good.\nThrough a thought-provoking talk\, guided reflection\
 , and engaging discussion\, you will explore real-life situations and gain
  insights and practical tools to navigate the challenges of daily life.\nI
 n this workshop\, we will explore:\n• Why calm matters—and how to rema
 in steady within the chaos\n• The role of obstacles in daily life and gr
 owth\n• Building inner strength without losing compassion\n• Rising ab
 ove distraction\, superficiality\, and reactive living\n• Developing cla
 rity\, purpose\, and resilience\n• Serving family\, community\, and soci
 ety more wisely\n• Living as a responsible and courageous citizen\nIf yo
 u feel called to live with greater depth\, strength\, and peace in a chaot
 ic world\, this workshop is for you.\nCome discover how calm becomes stren
 gth\, strength becomes service\, and philosophy becomes a way of life!\nWe
  look forward to meeting you\,\nVolunteers of New Acropolis Toronto\n=====
 =======================\nEVENT DETAILS:\n🎟️ Tickets: Online ticket pu
 rchase required\n🕖 Arrival: Doors open at 7 pm — our volunteers will 
 welcome you at the entrance. The workshop begins at 7:15 pm\, so we encour
 age you to arrive early to check in and settle in\n📍 Location: The work
 shop will be held at Alternity café\, a two-minute walk from the St. Geor
 ge subway station (exit on the St. George side).\n🪪 Check-In: Have your
  Eventbrite ticket handy (with your name and barcode). For security\, tick
 ets must include your full name\, and ID may be requested.\n📝 What to B
 ring: A pen and notebook—perfect for jotting down insights and reflectio
 ns you will want to remember.\n❓ Questions? Email us anytime at toronto@
 newacropolis.ca.\n📱 Last-minute help: On the day of the workshop\, the 
 best way to reach us would be by texting 647-317-1416.
LOCATION:Alternity
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/master-the-art-of-calm-within-the-chaos-
 toronto-3/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
