BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Next Chapter  -  Toronto World Premiere Screening  -   Live Pa
 nel Q&A
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260617T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260617T203000
UID:blogto-234849@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/09/original_image86e8ecf9-2999-46b9-a722-4b0c37dc42
 b5.jpg
DESCRIPTION:The Next Chapter has its Toronto world premiere on June 18 at 
 The Royal Theatre\, followed by a live post-screening panel discussion and
  audience Q&A.\nThe documentary explores healing\, psilocybin-assisted the
 rapy\, and the human stories behind a rapidly growing conversation in Cana
 da around mental health\, access\, and emerging treatment pathways. While 
 the film follows people in the second half of life\, the themes are much b
 roader and relevant to anyone thinking about depression\, grief\, caregivi
 ng\, healing\, or how this conversation is evolving in public life.\nWhat 
 makes the evening especially compelling is that it is more than a screenin
 g. The post-film discussion is designed to carry the conversation beyond t
 he movie itself\, bringing together community voices\, clinicians\, lived-
 experience perspectives\, and broader public interest in one room. Confirm
 ed panel participants include filmmaker Scott Wright\, Dr. Joshua Rosenbla
 t of UHN\, and Dr. Blake Pearson\, whose family’s story was recently fea
 tured in national CBC coverage as part of Canada’s growing public conver
 sation around psilocybin-assisted therapy.\nEvent Details\nDate: Thursday\
 , June 18\, 2026\nVenue: The Royal Theatre\, 608 College Street\, Toronto\
 nDoors Open: 6:00 PM\nScreening: 7:00 PM\nPost-Film Panel & Q&A: 7:45 PM\n
 Tickets: $20\nMore info and trailer: https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/the-next-
 chapter-documentary-world-premiere-screening-toronto-tickets-1987085514264
LOCATION:The Royal Theatre
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/the-next-chapter-toronto-world-premiere-
 screening-live-panel-qa-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Walrus Talks at Home: Education in Crisis
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260617T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260617T130000
UID:blogto-236287@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/09/original_imagee387aca3-7ba2-4fcf-b22e-fc5b4fbace
 81.jpg
DESCRIPTION:The UN Convention on the Rights of the Child affirms the right
  to education. Yet for millions of children who are refugees\, that promis
 e remains out of reach. Today\, 5.7 million of them are out of school\, an
 d the barriers grow as children get older\, limiting their opportunities f
 or stable\, self-determined lives.\nAt The Walrus Talks at Home: Education
  in Crisis\, speakers from Oxfam\, the Refugee Education Council\, Save th
 e Children\, and War Child will share powerful stories and practical insig
 hts on what it takes to help displaced children access education. From tea
 chers working outside traditional classrooms to local educators drawing on
  community history and customs\, they’ll examine what it takes to suppor
 t children in building a foundation for their future.\nHosted by Jennifer 
 Hollett\, Executive Director\, The Walrus\nFeaturing:\nDaria Meirut\, Comm
 unications Lead\, Refugee Education Council\nAlex Odongo\, Head of Program
 s\, War Child Canada\, Uganda\nArnold Okello\, Area Manager\, Oxfam in Uga
 nda\nKinfe Wubetu\, Program Manager\, Child Protection and Education\, Sav
 e the Children International Ethiopia
LOCATION:Virtual Event
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/the-walrus-talks-at-home-education-in-cr
 isis-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
