BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Butterflies On The Brink: The Story of the Mottled Duskywing Scree
 ning
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260618T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260618T200000
UID:blogto-234789@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/07/original_image27ca0df1-a8e6-4337-b3e0-0923049728
 10.jpg
DESCRIPTION:The Mottled Duskywing butterfly\, found only in a handful of h
 abitats in Ontario\, is vanishing at an alarming rate. Witness the inspiri
 ng efforts of a dedicated recovery team as they work tirelessly to bring t
 his species back to its former range.\nJoin us for a screening of Butterfl
 ies on the Brink: The Story of the Mottled Duskywing\, a gripping document
 ary about a rare butterfly species' fight for survival on the edge of exti
 nction.\nThe film is approximately 47 minutes\, followed by a Q&A panel wi
 th Miles Finlayson\, the director of Butterflies On The Brink\, with speci
 al guests:\nAdrienne Brewster\, Executive Director of Cambridge Butterfly 
 Conservatory.\nJessica Linton\, Senior Biologist and Species at Risk Manag
 er at Natural Resource Solutions Inc. and the Chair of the Ontario Butterf
 ly Species at Risk Recovery Team.\nDr. Ryan Norris\, professor at the Univ
 ersity of Guelph's Department of Integrative Biology\nPresented by the Dav
 id Suzuki Foundation\, a Canadian environmental non-profit organization wi
 th a mission to protect nature’s diversity and the wellbeing of all life
 \, now and for the future.\nFree. Registration required. Doors open at 6:1
 5 pm. At 6:30 pm\, seating becomes first-come\, first-served until capacit
 y is reached.\nThis program is part of TPL's Our Fragile Planet program se
 ries\, supported by Friends of Toronto Public Library\, South Chapter.​\
 nQuestions? Please contact North York Central Library - Business\, Science
  & Technology Department.\nThis program is also offered on Tuesday\, June 
 2\, 2026\, 6:30 pm – 8:00 pm at North York Central Library.\nYou can als
 o find more DSF programs at TPL.\nPlease register at the link.
LOCATION:Palmerston Library
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/butterflies-on-the-brink-the-story-of-th
 e-mottled-duskywing-screening-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
