BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:We Really Like Her! presents FRIED GREEN TOMATOES
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260618T181500
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260618T201500
UID:blogto-234140@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/24/original_image6eba9e26-04d6-48a6-8750-912b457ce9
 82.jpg
DESCRIPTION:This Pride season\, We Really Like Her! invites you to revisit
  the queer-coded equivalent of comfort food with a 35th anniversary screen
 ing of Fried Green Tomatoes.\nAdapted for the screen by author (and Match 
 Game superstar) Fannie Flagg and Carol Sobieski (Annie)\, this multi-gener
 ational dramedy follows unhappy housewife Evelyn (Kathy Bates) after a lif
 e-changing meeting with a charmingly wise stranger (Jessica Tandy as Ninny
 ) at an Alabama retirement home. Over the course of a variety of visits\, 
 Ninny tells Evelyn the epic love story of Idgie (Mary Stuart Masterson) an
 d Ruth (Mary Louise Parker)\, two women from different sides of the tracks
  who became business (and life) partners during the Great Depression. The 
 more time she spends with Ninny (and Idgie and Ruth)\, the more Evelyn is 
 inspired to step out of her comfort zone and into a new era of empowerment
 .\nAt times Fried Green Tomatoes is as juicy as its name suggests\, with h
 ighlights including an unforgettable murder mystery subplot and a sexy foo
 d fight. But the secret sauce truly is its four leading ladies\, all of wh
 ich will make you laugh as much as they make you cry uncontrollably. This 
 is a film that celebrates growth at all ages and stages of life\, serving 
 as a friendly reminder that it’s never too late to stand up for what\, o
 r who\, you believe in.\nCONTENT WARNING: This film features graphic depic
 tions of racism and domestic violence. Viewer discretion is advised.
LOCATION:Revue Cinema
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/we-really-like-her-presents-fried-green-
 tomatoes-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:2026 Sharelicious Asia - Toronto
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260619T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260619T230000
UID:blogto-236412@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/11/original_imagea28d111b-87c5-451f-8772-69ca908828
 3b.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Toronto’s First Asian-Inspired Summerlicious Launches: Share
 licious Asia Brings Together GTA Asian Restaurants for a Summer Food Celeb
 ration\nLead Paragraph\nEvery year\, Summerlicious inspires thousands of T
 orontonians to discover new dining destinations. Yet despite the city's vi
 brant and diverse Asian food scene\, Asian restaurant brands have never ha
 d a large-scale collective promotion platform of their own.\nThis summer\,
  SharEat — the world's first dining social platform founded by a Hong Ko
 ng entrepreneur — is launching Canada's first Asian-inspired Summerlicio
 us event: Sharelicious Asia 2026 - Toronto.\nRunning from June 19 to July 
 3\, 2026\, the two-week festival will bring together Asian restaurants acr
 oss Toronto and the GTA\, offering exclusive set menus and community-drive
 n experiences that encourage residents to discover some of the city's most
  unique and authentic Asian dining destinations.\nFounder Quote\n"Toronto 
 is home to one of the most diverse and exciting Asian food scenes in North
  America\, yet many outstanding restaurants remain undiscovered by a broad
 er audience. Through Sharelicious Asia\, we hope to inspire people to redi
 scover Toronto's Asian culinary culture over the course of two weeks."\nTh
 e festival will feature a wide range of Asian dining concepts across Toron
 to and the GTA\, including Hong Kong-style cafés\, Japanese and Korean cu
 isine\, Taiwanese restaurants\, and Southeast Asian eateries. Through limi
 ted-time menus\, community sharing\, and digital content promotion\, Share
 licious Asia aims to showcase the diversity and cultural influence of Asia
 n cuisine within the city.\n"Sharelicious Asia is more than a short-term d
 ining promotion. We envision it as a community movement that celebrates To
 ronto's Asian food culture. Our goal is to help more local residents disco
 ver Asian restaurant brands while positioning Asian cuisine as an integral
  part of Toronto's mainstream food culture."\nUnlike traditional restauran
 t promotions\, Sharelicious Asia integrates social media engagement\, comm
 unity interaction\, and user-generated content to redefine the dining disc
 overy experience. In addition to exclusive menus and dining offers\, the c
 ampaign will encourage restaurant reviews\, food sharing\, and community p
 articipation across Instagram\, Facebook\, Threads\, Xiaohongshu (RED)\, a
 nd the SharEat App\, creating greater conversation and engagement througho
 ut the festival.\nAbout SnapEat and SharEat\nSnapEat is a Canadian Asian f
 ood content platform founded by a Hong Kong entrepreneur. Across Instagram
 \, Facebook\, Threads\, and Xiaohongshu\, the platform has built a communi
 ty of approximately 20\,000 followers and generates more than 1 million or
 ganic views per month.\nEarlier this year\, the team also launched SharEat
 \, a world-wide first-in-Toronto Asian dining social platform that combine
 s restaurant discovery\, user-generated reviews\, ratings\, and community 
 interaction. The platform aims to build a thriving local Asian and Chinese
  food community across Canada.\nThe organizer hopes that Sharelicious Asia
  will gradually evolve into Toronto's signature annual summer celebration 
 of Asian food culture\, further strengthening connections among local Asia
 n restaurants\, content creators\, and food-loving communities.\nEvent Inf
 ormation\nEvent Name: Sharelicious Asia 2026 - Toronto\nEvent Dates: June 
 19 – July 3\, 2026\nEvent Highlights:\nSelected restaurants will offer e
 xclusive three-course lunch or dinner set menus starting from CAD $15\nPar
 ticipating Restaurants & Promotional Offers:\nhttps://snapeat.ca/sharelici
 ous-asia-toronto-campaign/\n(Official restaurant name list and menu link w
 ill be released on Jun 12\, 2026)\nSharelicious Asia QR code link:\nhttps:
 //drive.google.com/file/d/1vQU5Vz6RK-TZyI152i4KxWvZClvXox5L/view?usp=share
 _link\nSharEat APP link:\nApp Store: https://apps.apple.com/ca/app/shareat
 -social-food-map/id6753770558\nGoogle Play: https://play.google.com/store/
 apps/details?id=com.snapeats.app\nMedia Inquiries\nSnapEat / SharEat Team\
 nEmail: marketing@snapeat.ca\nInstagram: @snapeat.ca\nInstagram: @shareat.
 ai\nParticipating Restaurants\n(Listed in no particular order and particip
 ant list is continuously updating)\n• Wing Shing Cart Noodle\n• KUROKI
  IZAKAYA\n• Cheeky Chat Eatery\n• Ming Cuisine\n• Cafe le Majestik\n
 • Hoja Lamb Clay Pot & Stir-Fry\n• Hinode Udon and Tempura\n• Nanyan
 g Kopitiam Cafe\n• GOGO KIMBAP\n• INAROY\n• Shine Kitchen\n• Good 
 Catch Cafe\nSharEat Editor’s Featured Limited Time Menus\n(All offers ar
 e available during regular lunch and dinner hours on weekdays and weekends
 . Reservations may be required at selected restaurants. Please visit our w
 ebsite or download the SharEat Dining Social App for full details.)\nFeatu
 red Japanese Restaurant Menus\n$15 All-Day Set Menu (Regular Price: $20.98
 )\nMenu A\nChilled Lemon Udon with Shrimp Tempura\nSoft Drink\nChoice of S
 ide Dish ((Choose One): Seaweed Salad / Shrimp Tempura (2 pcs) / Duck Brea
 st (3 pcs) / Japanese Fried Chicken / Karaage (3 pcs)\nMenu B\nDuck Breast
  Udon Soup\nSoft Drink\nChoice of Side Dish ((Choose One): Seaweed Salad /
  Shrimp Tempura (2 pcs) / Duck Breast (3 pcs) / Japanese Fried Chicken / K
 araage (3 pcs)\n$20 All-Day Set Menu (Regular Price: $28.97)\nTempura Rice
  Bowl\nSparkling Strawberry Matcha\nChoice of Side Dish ((Choose One): Sea
 weed Salad / Shrimp Tempura (2 pcs) / Duck Breast (3 pcs) / Japanese Fried
  Chicken / Karaage (3 pcs)\nFeatured Thai Restaurant Menus\n$20 All-Day Se
 t Menu (Regular Price: $27.99–$28.99)\nMenu A\nThai Spicy Seafood Salad\
