 c9.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Church on Tap is a FREE monthly and affirming Anglican worship
  service for LGBTQ+ Christians & allies.\nHAPPY PRIDE!!\nChurch on Tap is 
 excited to celebrate all of God's Queer family and friends at our annual P
 ride worship service on Friday June 19th at Christ Church Deer Park. Servi
 ce begins at 7pm\, and will be followed by Drag Performances by our good f
 riends Carlotta Carlisle and Bella Bimbo at 8:30pm. Food and beverage (alc
 oholic and non-alcoholic) will be provided. Donations are gratefully accep
 ted.\nAs if a Drag Show and fabulous food and drink wasn't reason enough t
 o stay for the party\, we'll also be giving out prizes for a few lucky fol
 ks who choose to stick around. Don't miss out! You could be the proud reci
 pient of a gift card from a few fabulous\, Queer-owned businesses!\nOur se
 rmon will be given by Rev. Leigh Kern (she/they)\, Right Relations Coordin
 ator with the Anglican Diocese of Toronto\, leading our Diocese's reconcil
 iation efforts\, treaty relationship renewals\, and Indigenous justice ini
 tiatives. The Rev. Canon Alison Falby will co-lead the service.\nWorship w
 ill be led by Deb Whalen-Blaize\, accompanied by a few friends.
LOCATION:Christ Church Deer Park
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/church-on-tap-pride-celebration-worship-
 service-drag-performance-toronto/
