BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Toronto Jazz Festival 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260619T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260619T235900
UID:blogto-236354@blogto.com
DESCRIPTION:The Toronto Jazz Festival returns June 19 to 28 for its 39th e
 dition\, transforming Yorkville and venues across Toronto with ten days of
  live music\, free outdoor performances\, educational programming and inte
 rnational artists.\nWHO:\nThis year's festival features an extraordinary l
 ineup of internationally acclaimed artists spanning jazz\, global music\, 
 soul\, funk\, hip hop and beyond.\nHighlights include Grammy Award winning
  vocalist Cassandra Wilson\, celebrated for her genre defying blend of jaz
 z\, blues and folk\; French Lebanese trumpet virtuoso Ibrahim Maalouf\, on
 e of the world's most innovative and bestselling instrumental artists\; Ja
 panese piano phenomenon Hiromi's Sonicwonder\, renowned for breathtaking t
 echnical brilliance and explosive live performances\; and London's acclaim
 ed Kokoroko\, whose rich fusion of Afrobeat\, jazz and West African influe
 nces has made them one of the most exciting bands on the global scene.﻿ 
 ﻿\nAudiences can also experience the boundary pushing sounds of viral ja
 zz stars DOMi & JD Beck\, the genre bending energy of New Orleans favourit
 es The Soul Rebels\, the visionary jazz and hip hop explorations of Grammy
  nominated drummer and producer Kassa Overall\, and the deeply expressive 
 artistry of Israeli trumpeter Avishai Cohen's Big Vicious.\nCanadian highl
 ights include multiple Juno Award winner and Grammy nominee Laila Biali\, 
 acclaimed Montréal pianist and composer Gentiane MG\, and the Atlantic Ja
 zz Collective\, which welcomes legendary British vocalist Norma Winstone.\
 nFrom the gypsy jazz mastery of Stéphane Wrembel to groundbreaking contem
 porary sounds from around the world\, the Toronto Jazz Festival offers ten
  days of unforgettable musical discovery.\nWHEN: June 19 to 28\, 2026\nWHE
 RE: Yorkville Festival Hub\, Village of Yorkville Park\, The Rex Hotel\, K
 oerner Hall\, Danforth Music Hall\, Jazz Bistro\, Hugh’s Room Live\, The
  Pilot Tavern\, and venues throughout Toronto.\nWHY: As Toronto welcomes v
 isitors from around the world this summer\, the Festival presents nearly 6
 0 free performances alongside major ticketed concerts\, showcasing artists
  from Canada and across the globe.
LOCATION:Multiple Venues
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/toronto-jazz-festival-2026-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
