BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Considering Matthew Shepard
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260620T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260620T203000
UID:blogto-235095@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/15/original_image9051fa6d-682b-442b-9a1a-8708d314e0
 80.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Modern Sound Collective presents Considering Matthew Shepard\,
  a genre-defying oratorio by composer Craig Hella Johnson. The work offers
  a deeply human perspective on the tragedy of Matthew Shepard’s murder. 
 Through a wide range of musical styles and texts\, including poetry\, jour
 nalistic accounts\, sacred writings\, and reflections from Shepard’s par
 ents\, the work asks listeners to consider not only what was lost\, but wh
 at kind of world we are responsible for building in its wake. Tickets: mod
 ernsoundcollective.ca.
LOCATION:Metropolitan United Church
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/considering-matthew-shepard-toronto-2/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dance Division One Year Anniversary Party - 4AM LAST CALL
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260620T220000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260621T050000
UID:blogto-235759@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/29/original_image673c34af-6676-42d3-a9e0-d589a001c3
 c3.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Wow! A full year of DANCE DIVISION! We can’t thank you all e
 nough for showing up\, bass-facing and sweating your asses off with us eve
 ry month. It has been amazing to watch our dance floor grow into a loving 
 community where friendships have been forged and new connections establish
 ed. We couldn’t have done it without you.\nWe have loved bringing you su
 ch a wide range of local talented selectors\, newbies to veterans\, queer 
 family and allies. We will continue our ethos of brining folks together wi
 th the sole goal of dancing all night! On the dancefloor we are all equal\
 ; dancing is cathartic\, nostalgic\, we want to make you feel the music as
  much as it makes you dance.\nA HUGE thank you to our home venue\, Wiggle 
 Room. The staff\, security and of course our Captain Wiggle\, Takin\, for 
 giving us the opportunity to grow our roots in a safe space.\nTo celebrate
  this momentous occasion\, we have drawn from our alumni performers over t
 he year\, and we put them in a name picker to build this exquisite line up
 :\nMy Girl Tuesday to open the night (come early!).\nBR House\, bringing u
 s banging flavour from their home of Samba\, Brazil.\nHEATER\, back by pop
 ular demand! Will carry on the fire.\nHere’s where the surprises are:\nN
 our + Rami Aburob\nRami aburob + Dick Diamonds\nDick Diamonds + Barroness\
 nBarroness + Nour\nSet times:\n10 – 11: @mygirltuesdaydjs\n11 – 12 @br
 house.to\n12 – 1 @heatermusic\n1 – 2 @nour_toronto + @djaburob\n2 – 
 3 @djaburob + @ddiamonds4x4\n3 – 4 @ddiamonds4x4 + @barronessofficial\n4
  to close @Barroness + @nour_toronto\nWith our awesome VJ Prabin and his s
 ick visuals\, all night!\nCan’t wait to celebrate with you!\nYour hosts:
  Nour + Rami + Ellen + Wiggle Room\n#DANCEDANCEDANCE\nBehave. You know wha
 t to do and not to do.
LOCATION:Wiggle Room Toronto
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/dance-division-one-year-anniversary-part
 y-4am-last-call-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dope Comedy Pride Special
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260620T203000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260620T220000
UID:blogto-235752@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/29/original_image1f993206-58d0-4235-a1ab-8722ad1c7e
 00.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate Pride with big laughs and strong drinks! Put on your
  flashiest outfit to giggle and dance the night away. See you there🌈\nW
 e all need a laugh these days. Why not get it at Toronto’s hottest comed
 y party? Dope Comedy is the only black and queer run comedy show in a Turk
 ish Restaurant. Join 6 of Toronto’s best comedians\, the city’s hottes
 t DJ\, and 70 others for this inclusive night of fun! - @ The Comedy Lab i
 nside Sultan Ahmet\nSponsores have teamed up to create amazing raffle priz
 es! Other surprise sponsors may provide door giveaways and more.\nThis mon
 th we celebrate the bounty of comedic talent here in Toronto. We’ve brou
 ght together some of the funniest comics in the 6ix.\nDon’t miss this ni
 ght of Comedy\, Prizes\, and Partying. We'll have giveaways from sponsors\
 , champagne for the after party\, and the dopest DJ in the city. This show
  will sell out fast. Get your tickets before they’re gone!\nFor 1 Night 
 Only\, see Toronto’s hottest lineup of killer comics featured on CBC Rad
 io\, Sirius XM\, JFL 42\, JFL Montreal\, 420 Fest\, and more! Dance the ni
 ght away with Toronto’s hottest mix master. This show is like no other i
 n a gorgeous space that looks like a work of art.\nDrink\, Laugh\, Dance\,
  and Mingle with comics during the Afterparty. Bring your friends\, partne
 r\, or grandma\; anyone of legal drinking age that loves fun.\nThe Pre-par
 ty starts when the doors open at 8 pm. The DJ will be spinning the beats t
 o set the mood for the night. Show up early\, grab some drinks\, and explo
 re the beautiful art. After a drink or three\, the show begins at 8:30. La
 ughs continue until around 10:30 when the DJ will keep us dancing with a m
 ix of Hip-Hop and EDM.\nWerd Entertainment is a Black & Queer -run product
 ion and event group focused on highlighting unique voices\, telling new st
 ories\, and challenging traditional narratives. Founded by Danton Lamar\, 
 Werd Entertainment works to create and cultivate new spaces and ways to sh
 owcase the breadth and beauty of diversity in all of its forms.\nGet your 
 Tickets Now
LOCATION:The Comedy Lab
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/dope-comedy-pride-special-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
