BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Queer Asynchronies
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260620T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260620T170000
UID:blogto-236187@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/06/original_image5e9e443d-8345-456a-84ed-c94edee0fd
 ff.jpg
DESCRIPTION:June 18 – July 25\, 2026\nOpening Reception: Saturday\, June
  20\, 2–5 pm\nUnited Contemporary\, 129 Tecumseth Street\, Toronto\nUnit
 ed Contemporary is pleased to present Queer Asynchronies\, a group exhibit
 ion curated by Adrien Sun Hall\, opening in June to coincide with Pride To
 ronto. Bringing together the work of eight 2SLGBTQIA+ contemporary artists
 \, the exhibition explores themes of rebirth\, transformation\, and queer 
 timescapes.\nCurated by Adrien Sun Hall\, Queer Asynchronies features the 
 work of Steven Beckly\, Camille Charbonneau\, Rami George\, Dylan Glynn\, 
 Jordan King\, Natia Lemay\, Oluseye\, Ry Van Der Hout.\nThrough painting\,
  photography\, sculpture\, installation\, video and interdisciplinary prac
 tices\, Queer Asynchronies considers how queer and trans lives unfold in r
 elation to time\, through cycles of becoming\, acts of self-invention\, an
 d alternative temporalities that resist linear narratives. The exhibition 
 reflects on transformation as both a personal and collective process\, for
 egrounding experiences of renewal\,\nresilience\, and futurity.\nThe parti
 cipating artists engage with questions of identity\, memory\, embodiment\,
  and community\, offering perspectives that challenge normative understand
 ings of progress\, chronology\, and belonging.\nTogether\, their works pro
 pose queer temporalities as spaces of possibility\, where histories are re
 visited\, futures are imagined\, and the present becomes a site of continu
 ous reinvention.\nPresented during Pride Month\, the exhibition celebrates
  the breadth and vitality of contemporary queer and trans artistic practic
 es while creating space for reflection on the many ways queer communities 
 navigate time\, transformation\, and becoming.
LOCATION:United Contemporary
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/queer-asynchronies-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Queer Toronto Magazine Pride Open Mic Fundraiser Event
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260620T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260620T233000
