BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Summer Music in the Garden
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260621T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260621T200000
UID:blogto-234383@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/29/original_image09d58c3b-383c-4883-9abe-90f119c692
 57.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Summer Music in the Garden is an intimate live music experienc
 e by the waterfront\, occurring Thursdays at 7pm and Sundays at 4pm all su
 mmer. Presenting a multicultural slate of songs\, sounds and stories\, the
  Toronto Music Garden will host 20 free performances by Canadian musicians
  and celebrated local artists. This season’s highlights include the clas
 sical storytelling of JUNO nominee Julie Lumsden\, the Afrocentric choral 
 music of The Nathaniel Dett Chorale\, the electric Cuban rhythms of Montan
 o Cubano and the Western\, classical and Persian fusion of Ladom Ensemble.
 \nFull lineup:\nJune 21: The Sovereignty of Song featuring Julie Lumsden\n
 June 25: Garden Rhythms: Taiko Among the Trees featuring Nagata Shachu Jap
 anese Taiko and Music Group\nJune 28: And Still We Sing… Walk Together\,
  Children featuring The Nathaniel Dett Chorale\nJuly 2: Sofreh Tisch featu
 ring Ladom Ensemble\nJuly 5: Paisajes Argentinos featuring El Ceibo\nJuly 
 9: Most Definitely Toronto Music featuring Alex Lukashevsky and Mayme Joac
 h\nJuly 12: Bringing The Heat featuring Montuno Cubano\nJuly 16: From the 
 Highlands to the Heartland featuring Duncan Cameron\nJuly 19: Acalypha fea
 turing Labyrinth Ensemble\nJuly 23: Summertime Swing featuring The Sweet H
 ots\nJuly 26: Rhythm Speaks Many Languages featuring Agneya\nJuly 30: It
 ’s A Gut Feeling featuring Arparla and Elixir Baroque Ensemble\nAugust 2
 : Gather Ye Rosebuds featuring Rosebud String Quartet\nAugust 6: It’s A 
 Groove Thing featuring The Heavyweights Brass Band\nAugust 9: Where I Am I
 s What I Need featuring Tara Kannangara and Chris Pruden\nAugust 13: Songs
  of Stolen Children featuring Daughters of Donbas\nAugust 16: You Don’t 
