BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:TSA Walking Tour: New Meets Old
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260621T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260621T120000
UID:blogto-236415@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/11/original_imagedcc36abd-dfa8-4034-b5a3-02eff9eebc
 83.jpg
DESCRIPTION:With over 150 years of architectural history and home to over 
 80 heritage designated buildings\, the University of Toronto’s St. Georg
 e campus is without a doubt one of the most unique and remarkable architec
 tural collections in Canada. This historical campus though is far from a m
 useum. With just over 90\,000 students\, as well as thousands of faculty a
 nd staff\, the University is a city that is continuously growing and evolv
 ing–requiring new buildings\, retrofits and renovations to keep up with 
 its changing population.\nJoin us on a walk as we explore how architects h
 ave worked around\, added to\, repaired\, adapted and sometimes even reloc
 ated some of the university’s earliest structures. Learn about the uniqu
 e challenges and opportunities that arise when dealing with heritage struc
 tures. Along the way\, we will explore a range of buildings and landscapes
 —from High Victorian masterpieces with gleaming glass additions\, to Bru
 talist behemoths and modernist pioneers—many which challenge preconcepti
 ons about heritage and raise the question of how can we preserve our past 
 while meeting the needs of the future.\nMeeting Place: Steps of Weston Ent
 rance (Queens Park)\, Royal Ontario Museum\, 100 Queens Park\nFinish: Ziib
 iing\, Hart House Circle\nCost: $15 General Admission\, FREE for TSA Membe
 rs\nHost: Toronto Society of Architects
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/tsa-walking-tour-new-meets-old-toronto-3
 /
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
