 nd indie vendors. And it's a fundraiser!\nJoin us at Glad Day for this yea
 r's global screening event of Queer Cinema for Palestine's 2026 programmin
 g featuring six incredible short films by queer\, Palestinian\, and allied
  directors.\nHosted by ANNE ALIEN & Selena Vyle in partnership with the He
 lp Sondos Campaign\, featuring special guest speakers followed by Drag\, C
 omedy\, Burlesque and Live Music.\n6pm Doors\n7pm Comedy & Speakers\n8pm F
 ilm Screenings\n9pm Performances\n10:30pm Expected End\nAll proceeds fundr
 aised will be donated to the nights six film directors and the Help Sondos
  Campaign\, supporting a family of 13 in Gaza.\nShop local vendors\, win r
 affles\, and visit our partners to learn about their initiative and how to
  support their cause!\nSpeakers include\nKanna Worm\, Founder Help Sondos 
 Campaign\, with message from Sondos & family.\nJoey Nicholson-Landau and M
 arlee Wasser from Jews Say No To Genocide.\nDiana Chan McNally\, a City Co
 uncil candidate Ward 4\, .\nDaniela Bonamico\, a participant of Global Sum
 ud Flotilla.\nAll performance and speakers time donated for free in suppor
 t of the continued efforts to a liberated Palestine. All proceeds gathered
  will be donated transparently.\nCOVID PROTOCOLS\nWearing a mask is encour
 aged at this event.\nThe space has extra high (3 story) ceilings and there
  is a steady intake of outdoor air.\nUse your voice\, speak up\, come out!
 \nWe Dance in the Night\, and we Fight in the Day!
LOCATION:Glad Day Lit
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/queer-shorts-for-palestine-films-drag-ar
 tists-vendors-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
