ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/08/original_image3b2890a0-8be1-4bc3-a6d2-223f04296b
 f9.jpg
DESCRIPTION:This engaging 90-minute older adult-focused workshop breaking 
 down the four phases of filmmaking: pre-production\, production\, post-pro
 duction\, and marketing/distribution. Using real-world indie success stori
 es\, participants will learn how films are developed\, shot\, edited\, and
  brought to audiences worldwide — proving that creativity\, strategy\, a
 nd passion can turn even the smallest idea into a global project.\nNo film
  experience required! Program is free. Registration required.\nPresented b
 y Sean Cisterna\, award-winning filmmaker\, pioneers filmmaking workshops 
 for seniors 65+. He leads sessions across Canada\, including Ontario retir
 ement communities and festivals\, using accessible tools to spark creativi
 ty\, reduce isolation\, and build social bonds. He is the director of the 
 new documentary\, Silver Screamers\, opening at Toronto's Hot Docs Cinema 
 on April 3\, 2026. His past films include From the Vine\, Kiss and Cry\, a
 nd Full Out.
LOCATION:Toronto Public Library - Richview Branch
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/talk-with-film-director-sean-cisterna-fo
 r-older-adults-toronto/
