 2b.jpg
DESCRIPTION:MY HOUSE JUNCTION JAZZ FEST 2026: NICK MACLEAN 4-TET plays HER
 BIE HANCOCK\nAll Fest Tickets: www.eventbrite.com/cc/4844128\n@ My HOUSE\,
  2882 Dundas St. West\, Toronto\, 416-604-4555\nJune 22 to 28 -- 7 days of
  the nation's best jazz musicians in the Junction's own My HOUSE!\nFrom Pr
 ess Release:\nToronto's My HOUSE in the Junction live music venue & restau
 rant has again teamed up with Brooklyn\, NY's Browntasauras Records -- who
  has a studio in the Junction -- to bring you some of the best jazz in the
  country from June 22 to 28. This year again features Artist-In-Residence 
 BROWNMAN ALI as the fest's Artistic Director\, up from Brooklyn\, NY. This
  10x Global Music Award winner\, 12x JUNO Award nominee & GRAMMY Award lon
 g-lister will be on stage every night during the festival as either a side
 man or a leader\, and has hand-picked all the top-tier musicians & award-w
 inning ensembles involved in the 2nd annual My HOUSE Junction Jazz Fest fe
 aturing classic jazz\, modern jazz\, latin-jazz\, electric-jazz and more! 
 Come to My HOUSE in the Junction this June 22 to 28 for 7 nights of an unf
 orgettable jazz experience!\n----\nAll Fest Tickets: www.eventbrite.com/cc
 /4844128\n----\nFEST SCHEDULE AT-A-GLANCE -->\nMon-Jun-22\, 7pm: JORDANA T
 ALSKY: LIVE LOOPING\nTue-Jun-23\, 7pm: JACOB WUTZKE TRIO\nWed-Jun-24\, 7pm
 : NICK MACLEAN 4-TET play HERBIE HANCOCK\nThr-Jun-25\, 7pm: ARECIBO - Proy
 ecto Blanquito\nFri-Jun-26\, 8pm: BROWNMAN ELECTRYC TRIO\nSat-Jun-27\, 8pm
 : GENEVIEVE MARENTETTE's FLUX-STATE\nSun-Jun-28\, 4pm: MILES DAVIS: The PR
 ESTIGE YEARS\n----\nAll Fest Tickets: www.eventbrite.com/cc/4844128\n----\
 nWed-Jun-24\, 7:00pm\, $20 adv / $30 door\nNICK MACLEAN QUARTET plays HERB
 IE HANCOCK\nModern Jazz\nhttps://www.eventbrite.ca/e/1990305367933\nJUNO n
 ominated\, Global Music Award winning piano & synth wizard Nick Maclean ha
 s been deeply influenced by Herbie Hancock -- the legendary pianist & comp
 oser who revolutionized jazz through his work with Miles Davis’ Second G
 reat Quintet and as a pioneer of post-bop\, funk\, and synth-driven jazz. 
 This concert will feature the NICK MACLEAN QUARTET\, stacked with some of 
 Toronto's finest in a 2-set night featuring Herbie Hancock originals and M
 aclean's own Hancock-inspired compositions.\n:: Nick Maclean - piano\n:: B
 rownman Ali - trumpet\n:: Duncan Hopkins - bass\n:: Jacob Wutzke - drums\n
 www.NickMacleanJazz.com
