BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Reclaim Your Voice: Song Circle & Sound Bath for Women who have ex
 perienced Abuse & S.A.
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260624T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260624T203000
UID:blogto-236390@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/11/original_image8e737dd0-65e6-4453-9408-24487ef605
 b3.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Join song-carrier and certified music therapist Michaela for a
  community song circle to nourish the heart. At the beginning of every lin
 eage there was a fire\, a drum\, and a song. Elder and community song-lead
 er Laurence Cole reminds that “song is one of our most ancient technolog
 ies of belonging.” We gather to remember our innate connection to sound\
 , breath\, and rhythm. To play\, laugh\, cry\, and bow in reverence to our
  collective aliveness. This is a space to bring your joy\, your grief\, an
 d everything\nbetween. We will explore simple songs and juicy layered harm
 onies through the oral tradition of call and response. No prior experience
  with singing is necessary. Whether you are passionate for solo singing\, 
 campfire jams\, or someone who believes “I am not a singer\,” this spa
 ce is for you.\nThe gathering will close with a soothing sound bath to sup
 port integration and release. A sound bath is a full-body listening experi
 ence\, featuring live frequencies including crystal singing bowls\, voice\
 , drum\, and more. These vibrations have been shown to activate therapeuti
 c processes such as regulating the nervous system\, softening physical ten
 sion\, slowing the brainwaves\, and cultivating deep cellular rest.\nThis 
 session is planned to take place outdoors\, just prior to sunset. Please w
 ear what makes you feel most comfortable\, considering cozy layers and add
 itional props like blanket/mat\, journal\, water bottle\, insect repellent
 \, and a small pillow or folding chair for seating.\nOptional: bring one s
 mall item that connects you to the earth (stone\, feather\, flower\, fruit
 ) as we build a collective centrepiece of beauty to anchor us.
LOCATION:Corktown Common
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/reclaim-your-voice-song-circle-sound-bat
 h-for-women-who-have-experienced-abuse-sa-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:See You Downtown: Free Movie Nights Return This Summer
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260624T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260624T230000
UID:blogto-236300@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/09/original_image9477f121-ab1b-4518-960d-26e8336cca
 ec.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Downtown Movies in the Park returns to David Pecaut Square wit
 h six weeks of free outdoor screenings under the stars.\nPresented in part
 nership with TIFF\, this year’s series celebrates six timeless sports fi
 lms about underdogs and misfits on the unlikely road to victory\, defying 
 the odds and chasing their dreams.\nJoin us every Wednesday evening\, with
  pre-show programming beginning at 9:00 PM and films starting at 9:30 PM. 
 Each screening will include open captions and a film introduction by a TIF
 F programmer. Stage remarks will be translated by an ASL interpreter.\nThi
 s Summer’s Lineup:\nJune 24\nNext Goal Wins (2023)\nJuly 1\nCool Running
 s (1993)\nJuly 8\nA League of Their Own (1992)\nJuly 15\nThe First Slam Du
 nk (2022)\nJuly 22\nBend It Like Beckham (2002)\nJuly 29\nRemember the Tit
 ans (2000)\nGrab your friends\, bring a blanket or a chair\, and settle in
  for a movie night in the heart of downtown.
LOCATION:David Pecaut Square
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/see-you-downtown-free-movie-nights-retur
 n-this-summer-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Setting\, High Alpine Hut Network\, Shabason / Gunning
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260624T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260624T235900
UID:blogto-233814@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/17/original_imagee9513ded-ad5a-45d3-b2a2-cd032541a5
 ec.jpg
DESCRIPTION:SETTING\nThe North Carolina Piedmont-based trio of Setting bri
 ng together their substantial collective skills as musicians and their col
 laborative\, explorative mindsets from groups such as Mind Over Mirrors\, 
 Califone\, Black Twig Pickers\, Pelt\, Peeesseye\, Sylvan Esso\, and Jake 
 Xerxes Fussell to bear in their inventive and rich improvisations. Multi- 
 instrumentalists Jaime Fennelly\, Nathan Bowles and Joe Westerlund subvert
  expectations while creating a sense of ease and wonderment. Their intrica
 te interplay of synthesizers\, cassette loops\, banjo\, keyboards\, electr
 onics\, zithers\, and a litany of percussive instruments form a tactile am
 algam of celestial transcendence and terrestrial rhythm\, a loamy pulse fl
 uidly guiding every minute fluctuation in feel. Dedicated improvisers with
  years working together\, the band has developed their own idiosyncratic v
 ernacular and sense of flow. Setting’s self-titled album (Thrill Jockey)
  is a definitive statement of their improvisational acumen meeting composi
 tional rigor\, a robust wellspring of hypnagogic grooves and mosaiced text
 ures.  Setting harnesses the euphoria of communal creation.\nHIGH ALPINE H
 UT NETWORK\nHigh Alpine Hut Network is a psychedelic fusion group based in
  Toronto\, ON. The group has released 2 EP's & are currently working on th
 eir first full length album.\n"We are an improvising band that focus’ on
  immediate connection. As individuals\, we became stumped by our previous 
 groups solely performing worked out arrangements & decided to form a proje
 ct dedicated to intentional\, non-judgemental improvisations. Our common g
 oal is to honour the present moment & allow ourselves to change shape base
 d on the mood of the members\, the surroundings & the energy of the audien
 ce."\nSHABASON / GUNNING\nToronto dream-duo Joseph Shabason and Ben Gunnin
 g map fragmented cityscapes from bent electronics and late-night FM jazz t
 ransmissions.\nThe boys are back in town. After recording their debut in a
  remote cottage in Northern Ontario\, the duo relocated their jams to Shab
 ason’s Toronto studio where they gained unlimited access to a virtual co
 rnucopia of analog and digital gear and had the time to really push those 
 instruments to the brink. In the crisp autumnal sessions the duo conscious
 ly set out to make Ample Habitat with a fresh slate\; not a single melody 
 or patch was smuggled in on a USB stick. Fuelled with off-brand club soda\
 , the ethos was to infuse the sessions and the music itself with a sense o
 f discovery. Another perk of the new locale was being closer to friends an
 d neighbours\; TO music-scene luminaries Kieran Adams\, Bram Gielen\, and 
 Thom Gill dropped in\, rounding out a full jam band for the convivial B-si
 de surprise “Is Jubilee.” Although the album calls on a wild menagerie
  of digital voices\, the heart is warm and human\, favouring performance a
 nd play over presets and quantization. If J Dilla was able to teach an MPC
  jazz\, Shabason / Gunning aim to teach their hardware the ECM version.
LOCATION:The Jama
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/setting-high-alpine-hut-network-shabason
 -gunning-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
