BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Excellence and Resilience: Historical Mohawk Figures from Six Nati
 ons of the Grand River\, 1865-1965
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260625T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260625T200000
UID:blogto-236172@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/06/original_image50ee7cc6-9249-4504-9e23-39d6703805
 21.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Join Dr. Rick Monture as he ties together his family history w
 ith stories of influential Mohawk figures from Six Nations of the Grand Ri
 ver. Rick will reflect on the life of his grandmother\, Edith (Anderson) M
 onture—the first registered Indigenous nurse in Canada and veteran of th
 e First World War. He will also talk about his great uncle Gilbert Monture
 \, a veteran\, mining engineer\, and civil servant with connections to the
  Manhattan Project and the founding of Trent University. These stories wil
 l be contrasted with those of Rick’s maternal grandfather\, a residentia
 l school survivor\, farmer\, and lifelong reserve resident. Along the way\
 , Rick will discuss other influential figures\, including celebrated athle
 te Tom Longboat and noted physician Oronhyatekha (Peter Martin).\nRick Mon
 ture is Mohawk from Six Nations of the Grand River and a professor of Engl
 ish & Cultural Studies and Indigenous Studies at McMaster University McMas
 ter University\nNo registration required. All are welcome.
LOCATION:Lillian H Smith library
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/excellence-and-resilience-historical-moh
 awk-figures-from-six-nations-of-the-grand-river-1865-1965-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
