ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/07/original_imagefa82c569-98b4-410a-83e9-6c8cd0d9a1
 89.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Dora Award-winning Toronto singer\, composer\, multi-instrumen
 talist and producer Kunlé announces June 26\, 2026 as the release date fo
 r his highly-anticipated new album ‘Kunlé – The Journey’ (via Distr
 oKid)\, and celebrates with a new lyric video for “So Dear” and his al
 bum release concert at Small World Centre in Toronto on Thursday\, June 25
 \, 2026.\nFacebook Event\; https://www.facebook.com/events/197140964707459
 6/.\nPre-save new album: https://ffm.to/kunle-thejourney.\nNew lyric video
 \, “So Dear” (track three): https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=k0ChZt-id1
 Q.\nWho are the performers at the concert\;\nKunlé on vocals\, guitar and
  piano\, plus band members Stephen San Juan on lead guitar\, Johnson Afola
 bi with talking drums and percussion\, Andrew Kerr on bass and Oluwadamila
 re Odede on drums. Special guest live performers will be Dipo (featured vo
 cals on track four on the new album\, “Ọ̀rọ̀ Kan”)\, and Toronto
 ’s Paakwesi and Nelson Sobral\, who played slide guitar on track three\,
  “So Dear.”\nWhere\; Small World Centre\, 180 Shaw St.\, Studio 101 (n
 orth of Queen St. W.)\, Toronto\, ON\, M6J 2W5.\nWhen\; Thursday\, June 25
 \, 2026. Doors at 7:00 p.m. / Show at 8:00 p.m.\nHow Much\;\nGeneral admis
 sion\, $30.00 – Includes seated admission and a handwritten thank you ca
 rd keepsake from Kunlé.\nSupporter ticket\, $45.00 – Includes seated ad
 mission\, and a limited-edition red coral bead bracelet handcrafted by Kun
 lé and a handwritten thank you card.\nHis sophomore album ‘Kunlé – T
 he Journey’ will be released on digital and vinyl formats and features s
 even deeply rooted\, personal songs.\nThe songs on ‘Kunlé – The Journ
 ey’ were recorded in Kunlé’s home studio in Toronto and at Catherine 
 North Studios in Hamilton\, ON. It was produced and mastered at Catherine 
 North with Kunlé as co-producer and Will Crann (Blue Rodeo\, Whitehorse\,
  Feist\, The Glorious Sons and more) as co-producer and recording engineer
 .\nKunlé states\, “My new album is a collection of reflections and expe
 riences gathered through time—built from love\, spirit\, heritage and th
 e journey of self-discovery. It is both a departure from the expected path
  and a return home.”\nMore artist information: https://kunlemusic.com.
LOCATION:Small World Centre
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/kunle-the-journey-album-release-concert-
 toronto-2/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
