 gto.com/events/2026/06/08/original_imageaa8e3ccb-925e-4a63-a717-1094e7491a
 f5.jpg
DESCRIPTION:What's on your guilty pleasures playlist? The Canadian Chamber
  Orchestra asked that question to its musicians and audiences\, and built 
 a concert around the answers.\nLRLP III brings the CCO's signature intimat
 e format back to Eglinton St. George's United Church for an evening of mus
 ic that's equal parts surprising\, joyful\, and seriously played. Expect n
 ew string arrangements of beloved music (too beloved??)\, delivered in a l
 iving-room atmosphere where the musicians introduce each piece from the st
 age and the audience is close enough to feel every note.\nThe program draw
 s on anonymous nominations from CCO musicians and a public survey\, shaped
  into a playlist that spans genres\, eras\, and a healthy range of musical
  guilty consciences. New arrangements were created specifically for this c
 oncert by composer Chris Thornburrow\, CCO musician Laurence Schaufele\, a
 nd Co-Executive Directors Andrew Ascenzo and Drew Comstock.\nAdmission is 
 by donation -- bring 2lbs of non-perishable food items for the Eglinton St
 . George's Food Pantry\, or a monetary donation at the door. All are welco
 me.\nThe Canadian Chamber Orchestra is a Toronto-based ensemble committed 
 to building a new kind of classical music culture -- intimate\, accessible
 \, and community-rooted.
LOCATION:Eglinton Saint George's United Church
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/living-room-listening-party-iii-guilty-p
 leasures-playlist-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
