BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Hutch & Friends Pride Edition
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260626T210000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260626T223000
UID:blogto-236274@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/09/original_image51c55146-b173-496c-b46e-3f4ea1f8f4
 cc.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Come celebrate Pride with some of Toronto's best queer comedie
 nnes!\nHost\nPaul Hutcheson is a queer comedic performer\, writer and prod
 ucer. His six solo shows have been produced numerous comedic solo shows wh
 ich have toured Canada and the United States\, playing to sold-out audienc
 es\, glowing reviews and awards. He produces monthly comedy events Hutch &
  Friends and Hutch’s Storytime in Toronto. His comedy album\, Call Me Hu
 tch\, is produced by Howl & Roar Records.  Please visit canuckhutch.com fo
 r more information.\nPerformers\nJonathan Barrie is a Toronto-based storyt
 eller and comedian who loves to share his (mis)adventures on stage. Traine
 d at Second City and Comedy Bar\, he takes audiences on hilarious\, heartf
 elt journeys. Catch him lighting up storytelling shows and open mics acros
 s the GTA.\nMartha Chaves is an award-winning stand-up comedian\, actor\, 
 writer\, and keynote speaker who has been making Canada laugh for over two
  decades. Martha tours coast to coast. In 2023\, she was part of the Gala 
 the Root of All Evil at the Winnipeg Comedy Festival\, which earned a Cana
 dian Screen Award nomination. She’s a regular on CBC’s Because News an
 d Laugh Out Loud and a veteran of Just For Laughs\, the Winnipeg Comedy Fe
 st and more.\nBased in Toronto\, Adrienne Fish has recorded four performan
 ces for national television\, including an appearance at Montreal's Just F
 or Laughs Festival as part of Canada's Homegrown Comics\, airing on CTV Co
 medy Channel and CraveTV. She has appeared on Season 2 of CTV's Roast Batt
 le Canada and is regularly featured across North America on Sirius XM radi
 o and was nominated for two Canadian Comedy Awards including Breakout Arti
 st of the Year.\nNile Seguin has performed at the Just for Laughs Festival
 \, San Francisco Sketchfest\, the Winnipeg Comedy Festival\, the Halifax C
 omedy Festival and the Boston Comedy Festival. A three-time Canadian Comed
 y Award nominee\, he has also opened for James Adomian\, Janeane Garofalo 
 and Hannibal Buress. Nile has written for Comedy Network’s The Beaverton
  as well as This Hour Has 22 Minutes\, Tallboys\, the Gemini Award winning
  The Hour. He was also nominated for a Canadian Screen Award for his writi
 ng on CBC’s Still Standing and most recently Nile his solo podcast Total
  Nileation.\nOften called clever\, unique and late for dinner Jordan Traff
 ord is a Toronto based comic with a self-deprecating style that can be bes
 t described by someone else. Most noted for his one liners and quirky word
  play Jordan recently realized being self-conscious sounds like being self
 -aware and likes that. When not performing Jordan can most likely be fo
LOCATION:Burdock
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/hutch-friends-pride-edition-toronto-2/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
