 39.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Customize your own kraft cover sketchbook with a linocut print
  of your own creation!\nIn this workshop\, you’ll be creating a custom l
 inocut image to print onto a sketchbook cover. Our instructor will guide y
 ou step-by-step\, in carving the lino\, inking the image\, and getting a c
 lean\, even print. By the end of the workshop\, you’ll leave with a uniq
 ue sketchbook\, fine art prints and the knowledge of how to set up a print
 making space at home. Beginners welcome.\nYou can create anything you wish
 \; please bring your own photos\, sketches and drawings for reference. We 
 will be carving a 4 x 6 inch lino block\, so your design needs to fit thos
 e dimensions.\nPrintmaking materials will be provided. We’ll also have P
 osca paint markers available for adding an extra punch of colour.\nMateria
 ls\n✸ 4x6 soft lino block\n✸ Kraft cover (5.5x8.25)\, lay flat\, 100gs
 m notebook\n✸ Akua ink\n✸ Brayers\n✸ Strathmore toned paper\nWho is 
 this for?\nJournalers\, artists and beginners looking for a lowkey worksho
 p\, with a finished product to keep all your creative ideas in one place.\
 nAbout your instructor\nArtist and conservationist\, Alan Li\, uses pencil
 s and paint to document the wonders of the natural world. Alan’s mission
  is to build connections to nature through art-based education. Since 2015
 \, he has been partnering with non-profit environmental organizations to t
 each nature focused art programs and workshops.\nSee more of his works her
 e: https://www.alanlidrawings.com/\nOverview:\n📔Guided instruction\n
 📔All materials provided\n📔Perfect for journalers\n📔Take home a cu
 stom notebook and stamp!
LOCATION:Gwartzman's Art Supplies
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/carve-print-custom-linocut-sketchbooks-t
 oronto/
