BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:EVERYTHING IS POLITICAL - SATIRE with CALE BAIN
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260628T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260628T150000
UID:blogto-236183@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/06/original_imagee549d767-0181-469a-8867-416fb5c063
 34.jpg
DESCRIPTION:It's part lecture\, part seminar\, part workshop.\nThe lecture
  part is an examination of satire\, a look at what it is\, what conditions
  are needed for it to exist\, what it can (or does not) achieve. It's part
  sociology\, part literature studies\, part comedy studies.\nThe seminar p
 uts pen to paper and gives people a chance to see how satire works by putt
 ing it into practice in groups using fairytale structures to challenge heg
 emonies\, looking at using familiar genres and tropes to interrogate patri
 archies and supremacies\, for testing power structures on the whole.\nFina
 lly\, after putting this stuff in on paper\, we get up and try to put it i
 nto place in scenes.\nSee\, the ultimate thesis is that every act is a pol
 itical one\, whether we're aware of the politics engaged in those acts or 
 not. I'm trying to get people to be aware and to try to say something clea
 r\, or be able to choose to say something clear if they're inclined to.\nC
 ale Bain was the founding Artistic Director of Improv Theatre Sydney and a
  journalism and comedy scholar from the University of Technology Sydney in
  Australia. He’s performed\, taught and directed improv all over the wor
 ld.\nBring a pencil and paper and a newspaper or magazine.\nCOST: $100 + T
 ax
LOCATION:Comedy Bar East
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/everything-is-political-satire-with-cale
 -bain-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
