 O - Proyecto Blanquito\nFri-Jun-26\, 8pm: BROWNMAN ELECTRYC TRIO\nSat-Jun-
 27\, 8pm: GENEVIEVE MARENTETTE's FLUX-STATE\nSun-Jun-28\, 4pm: MILES DAVIS
 : The PRESTIGE YEARS\n----\nAll Fest Tickets: www.eventbrite.com/cc/484412
 8\n----\nSun-Jun-28 (matinee)\, 4:00pm\, $20 adv / $30 door\nMILES DAVIS: 
 PRESTIGE YEARS feat. Brownman Ali\nClassic jazz\nhttps://www.eventbrite.ca
 /e/1990305482275\nHailed as “one of the greatest interpreters of Miles D
 avis' work in Canada” (Hamilton Spectator)\, multi award-winning trumpet
  iconoclast Brownman Ali explores Miles' work from '51 to '56\, where a st
 ring of groundbreaking albums for Prestige Records would be recorded\, inc
 luding Cookin’\, Relaxin’\, Workin’\, and Steamin’ -- blending beb
 op virtuosity with a cool\, lyrical sensibility. Brownman and a selection 
 of top-shelf jazz artists will explore these recordings channeling the int
 ensity and innovation of Miles’ early genius.\n:: Brownman Ali - trumpet
 \n:: Nick Maclean - piano\n:: Bennett Young - bass\n:: Frank Botos - drums
