BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Toronto Fringe Festival
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260630T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260630T230000
UID:blogto-236076@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/04/original_imagec9cd2c37-012b-436b-83a9-5012387ec6
 03.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Fringe is proud to announce programming for the 38th A
 nnual Toronto Fringe Festival\, taking place June 30-July 12\, 2026 with 1
 23 shows in 27 venues across the city. Tickets and passes are on sale now 
 at www.fringetoronto.com.\nChosen by lottery\, Toronto Fringe is the home 
 for first-time performers\, celebrated collectives\, TikTok stars taking t
 o the stage\, and award-winning theatre pros presenting their new works.\n
 The Toronto Fringe is Ontario’s largest performance festival with an ecl
 ectic mix of topics and themes including eight shows inspired by Shakespea
 re\, five shows from the Caribbean diaspora\, three magic shows\, two show
 s about Medical Assistance in Dying\, and a comedy show performed entirely
  in Mandarin.\nToronto Fringe will host performances at traditional theatr
 e spaces and pop-up venues spread out between Keele Street\, Davenport Ave
 nue\, Pape Avenue\, and Lake Ontario\, with dramatic theatre\, clown\, dan
 ce\, storytelling\, sketch comedy\, musicals\, improv\, puppets\, and stan
 d up\, plus six KidsFest shows\, and thirteen days of free community progr
 amming at the Festival Hub at Soulpepper.
LOCATION:Multiple Venues
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/toronto-fringe-festival-toronto-4/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Toronto Fringe Festival- Mary\, Mary
