 gto.com/events/2026/06/14/original_image767efe46-44f1-497b-955b-3ab040862d
 45.jpg
DESCRIPTION:A suitcase\, a dream\, and a one-way journey to London\, a you
 ng Caribbean woman leaves everything she knows behind in search of a brigh
 ter future. Running at Soulpepper Theatre’s Kevin & Roger Garland Cabare
 t from July 2 to July 11\, Sincerely\, E traces her journey through migrat
 ion\, love\, and the search for belonging. A love letter to the courageous
  immigrant spirit.\nSincerely\, E is infused with the iconic sounds of the
  late 1960s. Inspired by the legacy of the Windrush generation\, the play 
 honours and celebrates their lasting contributions to Toronto’s vibrant 
 Caribbean community.\nTickets available here - https://www.fringetoronto.c
 om/fringe/show/sincerely-e\nRelaxed Performances: July 6 & 9\nPay-What-You
 -Can Performances: July 7 & 9\nDebuting at the Toronto Fringe Festival\, S
 incerely\, E is made possible through Guild Festival Theatre’s Youth Eng
 agement Scarborough Initiative.
LOCATION:Soulpepper Theatre's Kevin & Roger Garland Cabaret
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/sincerely-e-debuts-at-toronto-fringe-fes
 tival-toronto/
