BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:MOMME DOMME
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260703T194500
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260703T203500
UID:blogto-236521@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/13/original_image5d218003-edd6-46f2-9bee-6c3a561b02
 cd.jpg
DESCRIPTION:You’re invited to an exclusive preview of How To Be A Domme 
 101\, hosted by performance artist and aspiring institutional darling Pegg
 y Mitchell.\nEach night\, four women arrive ready for a private mistresscl
 ass. From TikTok tarot readings to strap-on sashaying\, Momme Domme weaves
  sonic intervention\, ritual and voyeurism into an embodied surrender to t
 he matriarchy.\nPart workshop\, part intervention\, Momme Domme is a seduc
 tive and surreal theatre performance interrogating complicity\, artistic c
 onsumption and the commodification of the feminine body.\nDone asking if w
 e’re dating the same guy? Ready to surrender to the matriarchy?\nPresent
 ed as part of the Toronto Fringe Festival.\nCOMPANY\nBlemme Fatale Product
 ions\nCREATOR\nBlemme Fatale\nMORE ABOUT THE COMPANY\nBlemme Fatale Produc
 tions co-creates live performances and supplementary schools that uncover 
 hidden histories using Pan-African oral traditions. Boundless echoes\, jus
 t like your mama’s mama’s mama knows it.\nRUNTIME\n50 minutes\nCREDITS
 \nDramaturg / Artistic Support: Me Time\nStage Manager: Annabel Pearson\nS
 et Designer: Victoria van der Meulen\nPoster Design: Kiko Keighery\nCostum
 e Designer: Sol Nolan Lee\nMarketing Manager: Cindy Dzib\nCast: Elena Bapt
 iste\nCast: Barbara Indriliunas Snow\nCast: Kimmie Croscup\nACCESS\nLevel 
 of Physical Access: Accessible\nCOVID-19 POLICY\nMasks: Optional\nFACILITI
 ES\nAir Conditioned: Yes\nWashrooms: Yes\nOutdoors: No
LOCATION:Alumnae Theatre Mainspace
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/momme-domme-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Seasons of Souls - Keir Collective
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260703T203000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260703T213000
UID:blogto-236254@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/08/original_image9985fff4-c7ed-4f39-9645-d4f6b93c80
 51.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Seasons of Souls - Keir Collective\nToronto Fringe Festival 20
 26\nFactory Theatre Mainspace | July 3–11\, 2026\nCreated by the award-w
 inning team behind the 2024 Toronto Fringe Patron's Pick *Scenes From An I
 talian Restaurant* and the 2025 Best of Fringe production *The Iron Mask*\
 , *Seasons of Souls* is the debut production of Keir Collective.\nRooted i
 n contemporary ballet and cinematic movement storytelling\, this original 
 contemporary dance work explores transformation\, resilience\, grief\, joy
 \, connection\, and renewal through athletic choreography and immersive th
 eatricality. Centered around the concept of time\, Seasons of Souls asks a
  universal question: how do we spend our time\, and do we ever truly have 
 enough of it?\nFeaturing a dynamic cast of Toronto-based artists\, Seasons
  of Souls blends powerful movement\, evocative imagery\, and emotionally d
 riven storytelling into a visually striking theatrical experience.\nPerfor
 mance Dates\nJuly 3 – 8:30 PM\nJuly 4 – 12:30 PM\nJuly 5 – 3:30 PM\n
 July 7 – 9:15 PM\nJuly 9 – 5:45 PM\nJuly 10 – 10:00 PM\nJuly 11 – 
 6:45 PM\nVenue\nFactory Theatre Mainspace\n125 Bathurst Street\, Toronto\n
 Tickets: $15–20 (Toronto Fringe Festival pricing)\nFor tickets and more 
 information\, visit: https://fringetoronto.com/fringe/show/seasons-souls
LOCATION:Factory Theatre Mainspace
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/seasons-of-souls-keir-collective-toronto
 /
