BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Rob Godwin: Project Apollo
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260704T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260704T160000
UID:blogto-235997@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/03/original_imageece5a8c3-b3ca-4d6f-b2ad-0fa76449d0
 53.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a talk with Rob Godwin\, author and Research Direc
 tor at General Astronautics Research Corporation. Learn about the history 
 of the Apollo program\, the journey to get there\, and Godwin's involvemen
 t with the astronauts who walked on the moon!\nGodwin's talk will be follo
 wed by a live Q&A with the audience. Copies of his books will be available
  for sale and signing at the event.\nFree. All are welcome.\nRob Godwin is
  the award-winning author of over 100 books on space. He is also the found
 er of Apogee Books\, an imprint of Collector's Guide Publishing. Launched 
 in 1998\, the first Apogee title was "Apollo 8 The NASA Mission Reports". 
 It was published at the personal request of astronaut Buzz Aldrin. Godwin 
 was also the Space Curator at the Canadian Air & Space Museum. He is a lif
 etime member of the both the National Space Society and the Space Frontier
  Foundation and a member of the International Astronautical Federation and
  American Astronautical Society History Committees.
LOCATION:Merril Collection - Lillian H. Smith Library
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/rob-godwin-project-apollo-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
