BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Three Musketeers at Guild Festival Theatre's Family Fest
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260710T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260710T190000
UID:blogto-235947@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/03/original_image795c83f5-4459-4cc2-b8fd-4f2cd6d863
 da.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Guild Festival Theatre presents THE THREE MUSKETEERS\, created
  and performed by The Lakeside Players as part of Family Fest.\nYoung d’
 Artagnan arrives in Paris dreaming of adventure and soon joins forces with
  the legendary Musketeers Athos\, Porthos\, and Aramis. Together\, they mu
 st outwit the scheming Cardinal Richelieu and dangerous Milady de Winter i
 n a thrilling tale of friendship\, honor\, and daring heroics. This cast w
 as initially populated by a who’s who of Canadian theatre legends\, but 
 due to scheduling conflicts and creative differences\, this 18th century e
 pic with over twenty characters will be performed by two of Canada’s mos
 t enthusiastic and available performers. Will they be able to pull it off?
 !\nDon’t miss Alexandre Dumas’ classic\, ‘The Three Musketeers’!\n
 Recommended for ages 4+.\nJuly 10th-12th\, 6pm-7pm\nFree!\nGuild Festival 
 Theatre’s 2026 Season is presented by ARC Insurance & Financial Services
  Inc.
LOCATION:Guild Festival Theatre
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/the-three-musketeers-at-guild-festival-t
 heatres-family-fest-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Toronto Outdoor Art Fair returns July 10th at Nathan Philips Squar
 e
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260710T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260710T170000
UID:blogto-229835@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/01/27/original_imagef8f3911b-81f8-4399-a19a-b73ac621e7
 95.jpg
DESCRIPTION:In July 2026\, the Toronto Outdoor Art Fair (TOAF) celebrates 
 a landmark milestone: 65 years as Canada’s largest and longest-running j
 uried contemporary outdoor art fair.\nEach summer\, TOAF brings together o
 ver 400 visual artists and 170\,000 visitors at Nathan Phillips Square\, t
 ransforming Toronto’s civic heart into a vibrant gathering place for art
 \, conversation\, and discovery. This milestone year honours the long arc 
 of artistic careers and the enduring power of experiencing art together in
  public.
LOCATION:Nathan Philips Square
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/toronto-outdoor-art-fair-returns-july-10
 th-at-nathan-philips-square-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Toronto Summer Music: Fire & Resilience
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260710T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260710T213000
UID:blogto-235227@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/19/original_image381ce499-38e6-4e12-a102-6be0385cdf
 dc.jpg
DESCRIPTION:This programme traces a journey through solitude\, song\, and 
 survival. Bach’s radiant E Major Partita opens with brilliance and poise
 . American voices emerge in Copland’s beloved folk settings — simple\,
  tender\, and deeply human. Kelly-Marie Murphy’s Give Me Phoenix Wings T
 o Fly rises from devastation toward renewal\, and Shostakovich’s Piano Q
 uintet closes the evening with brooding intensity\, razor-sharp wit\, and 
 ultimately\, hard-won light — music of clarity\, courage\, and rebirth.
LOCATION:Walter Hall
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/toronto-summer-music-fire-resilience-tor
 onto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
