BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:TFS Presents a Jacques Demy Double Bill!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260712T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260712T170000
UID:blogto-235806@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/31/original_image81bf983a-6c0f-4f03-9b4f-a7662e209b
 c2.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Step into the world of Jacques Demy with a French double featu
 re that’s equal parts dreamy and devastating. Lola (1961) sets the tone 
 with Anouk Aimée in a performance that’s cool\, tender\, and unforgetta
 ble – a story of love and timing told with quiet elegance. Then The Umbr
 ellas of Cherbourg (1964) turns the dial all the way up: Catherine Deneuve
 \, Michel Legrand’s soaring music (including “I Will Wait for You”)\
 , and colours that practically glow as the romance deepens into heartbreak
 . Two masterpieces\, one filmmaker\, and a big-screen experience that’s 
 going to stay with you long after you leave the theatre!\nLola (1961)\nJac
 ques Demy’s Lola is French romance with a bittersweet edge – all\nchan
 ce meetings\, missed timing\, and lingering feelings. Anouk Aimée is\nmag
 netic in the title role\, bringing warmth and mystery to a character you\n
 can’t quite forget. Stylish\, wistful\, and quietly devastating in the b
 est way\,\nit’s a film that rewards the big screen - where the atmospher
 e and emotion\nreally settle in!\nThe Umbrellas of Cherbourg (1964)\nA can
 dy-coloured knockout of a musical where every line is sung\, The\nUmbrella
 s of Cherbourg is pure cinematic emotion. Catherine Deneuve is\nluminous a
 t the centre of it all\, and Michel Legrand’s score is the kind that\nge
 ts under your skin and stays there - including the unforgettable “I Will
 \nWait for You.” Romantic\, heartbreaking\, and visually electric\, this
  is one of\nthose films that feels made for a theatre - you don’t just w
 atch it\, you get\nwashed over by it.\nBuy your tickets here: https://para
 diseonbloor.com/purchase/534878/
LOCATION:Paradise Theatre
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/tfs-presents-a-jacques-demy-double-bill-
 toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:TSA Walking Tour: Downtown Yonge
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260712T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260712T153000
UID:blogto-236427@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/11/original_imageaf6052a3-a37f-4214-a37b-a761652f05
 5f.jpg
DESCRIPTION:No street is more iconically Toronto than Yonge Street.\nFirst
  surveyed in the late 18th century to aid trade and settlement\, Yonge has
  been both witness and protagonist in the story of Toronto’s development
  from a small colonial outpost to the multi-cultural city we see today. Bu
 sy\, diverse\, and slightly chaotic\, its cacophonous nature is the legacy
  of over 200 years of urban development\, with competing interests—enter
 tainment\, commerce\, residential\, education\, and more—all looking to 
 stake a claim on what has often been called Ontario’s Main Street.\nJoin
  us for a tour as we unpack this legacy through the buildings and landscap
 es of downtown Yonge. Focusing on five of its most recognizable and visite
 d blocks—from Queen to College—we’ll reveal this street’s many liv
 es through its surrounding spaces: from fragments of a now-lost 1800s neig
 hbourhood\, to the high- and low-brow entertainment venues that made Yonge
  synonymous with fun. Not to mention the currently sprouting supertalls ma
 king the most of their recognizable Yonge Street addresses. From landmark 
 structures to hidden gems\, architectural giants to small public art piece
 s\, this tour along Yonge is as diverse and storied as the street itself!\
 nMeeting Place: Church of the Holy Trinity\, 10 Trinity Square\nFinish: Co
 llege Park\nCost: Free!\nHost: Toronto Society of Architects
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/tsa-walking-tour-downtown-yonge-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Twelfth Night
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260712T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260712T213000
UID:blogto-235940@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/02/original_imaged252eb0a-73ff-4686-bad6-504fc13eb8
 9b.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Under the open sky of Toronto’s iconic High Park\, Shakespea
 re’s beloved romantic comedy comes to life. When Viola is shipwrecked an
 d disguises herself as a man\, she sets off a whirlwind of mistaken identi
 ties\, mischievous schemes\, and tangled romances.\nAs disguises unravel a
 nd hearts collide\, Twelfth Night delivers laughter\, music\, and the joyf
 ul chaos of love. Pack a picnic\, gather your friends\, and enjoy a summer
  night of theatre under the stars.
LOCATION:High Park Amphitheatre
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/twelfth-night-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Canadian Photography Conference 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260713T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260713T140000
UID:blogto-235607@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/27/original_imagea2186a75-f1a4-4f08-bd4c-aebc6d36e2
 e5.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Come experience how our shared love of photography can connect
 \, inspire\, and equip us to share our nation's stories at the Canadian Ph
 otography Conference 2026!\nJoin us July 13-16\, 2026\, in where the Footh
 ills Camera Club and the Canadian Association for Photographic Art are hos
 ting an unforgettable gathering of creativity\, artistry\, and community.\
 nThe schedule features speakers with diverse genres\, including a high-oct
 ane look at capturing split-second action from Olympian-turned-photographe
 r Kelly VanderBeek\, a deep dive into powerful documentary storytelling wi
 th Nadya Kwandibens\, and practical insights on using wildlife images for 
 activism with premier conservation photographer John E. Marriott. From Ric
 hard Martin’s abstract fine-art techniques and Monika Deviat’s mesmeri
 zing night sky masterpieces to Craig Hilts’ adrenaline-fueled prairie st
 orm chasing\, the event is packed with dynamic presentations\, trade shows
 \, and hands-on excursions designed to inspire creators of all skill level
 s.\nAttend Online\nFor the first time ever\, the conference is going hybri
 d!  You can still join virtually with live-stream access and 12 months of 
 on-demand recordings.\nThe Live-Stream option also allows real time transl
 ation through YouTube Live and Google Translate for attendees whose primar
 y language is not English.
LOCATION:Virtual Event
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/canadian-photography-conference-2026-tor
 onto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
