BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:TSA Walking Tour: Harbourfront
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260726T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260726T120000
UID:blogto-236410@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/11/original_image62b78bb6-c120-42bf-9ccf-ca65faab58
 47.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Not too long ago\, Toronto central harbourfront was a place of
  merchants and industry—dominated by warehouses\, factories and truck ga
 rages. But look around today and what you’ll see is a place full of whim
 sical landscapes and cultural spaces that make our central waterfront one 
 of the city’s most interesting places to be.\nJoin us on a tour as we ta
 ke a walk along the quays\, slips and docks of Harbourfront\, Toronto’s 
 pioneer neighbourhood in waterfront revitalization\, and uncover the stori
 es of this multi-decade transformation through its buildings and landscape
 s. Along the way we will see how old industrial buildings and spaces have 
 been transformed into some of the city’s leading cultural venues and tak
 e a look at award winning residential projects and imaginative landscapes 
 reconnecting Torontonians with their lake. From artist studios to manicure
 d gardens\, wetlands to grain silos\, there is so much to see at the water
 front!\nMeeting Place: Plaza on North side of Queen’s Quay Terminal (207
  Queens Quay Street W)\nFinish: West end of Music Gardens\nCost: $15 Gener
 al Admission\, FREE for TSA Members\nHost: Toronto Society of Architects
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/tsa-walking-tour-harbourfront-toronto-3/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
